[SWS_LBAP_00023] StdCppImplementationDataType. category ==ASSOCIATIVE_MAP without an Allocator
⌈
Kind:
type alias
Header file:
#include "{<namespace-derived-directory-path-lower>}/impl_type_{<shortname-lower>}.h"
Scope:
namespace {<hierarchical-namespace-list-lower>}
Symbol:
{<symbol-assocmap>}
Syntax:
using {<symbol-assocmap>} = ara::core::Map<{<assocmap-key-type>},
{<assocmap-value-type>}>;
Description:
For each StdCppImplementationDataType. category ==ASSOCIATIVE_MAP without an
Allocator there shall exist a C++ type alias. The storage is managed by the default allocator
std::allocator [12].
{<symbol-assocmap>}
as per {<symbol-string>} in [SWS_LBAP_00015]
{<assocmap-key-type>}
as per {<containerized-type>} in [SWS_LBAP_00008]. Refer to [12]
for requirements on {<assocmap-key-type>}
Descriptors:
{<assocmap-value-type>
}
as per {<containerized-type>} in [SWS_LBAP_00008]
Example:
// Example: map<typeref,string>
using T_M_IPX_TR = ara::core::String;
// modelled TYPE_REF
using T_M_IPX_T1 = ara::core::String;
// generated
using T_M_IPX =
ara::core::Map<
T_M_IPX_TR,
// inplace==undef
T_M_IPX_T1
// inplace==FALSE
>;
See also:
[TPS_MANI_03183], [TPS_MANI_03184], [TPS_MANI_03185], [SWS_CORE_01400]
